{% doc %}
  A horizontal rule between things.

  Four styles, and the fourth is why this is a snippet rather than a CSS class:
  a wave is an SVG, and an SVG needs its colour and height written into it at
  render time.

  ## Why the wave is inline SVG and not a background image

  A `background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,…")` cannot inherit `currentColor`,
  so its colour has to be URL-encoded into the data URI — which means a merchant
  changing the divider colour produces a completely new image the browser has to
  parse again. Inline SVG takes `fill` from a custom property, so the same markup
  recolours instantly and costs nothing.

  It is `aria-hidden` and carries no `role`. A divider is a visual separator: a
  screen reader announcing "separator" between every section is noise, and the
  heading structure already tells someone where they are. When a divider is
  genuinely semantic — the end of one topic and the start of another — the
  section around it should be an `<hr>` or a landmark, not this.

  @param {string} [style] - solid | dashed | dotted | wave. Default solid
  @param {string} [color] - Defaults to the theme divider colour
  @param {number} [thickness] - Pixels. Ignored by the wave, which scales
  @param {string} [width] - full | container | short. Default full
  @param {boolean} [flip] - Mirrors the wave vertically

  @example
    {% render 'divider', style: 'wave', color: settings.divider_color %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign divider_style = style | default: 'solid'
  assign divider_color = color | default: settings.divider_color | default: '#e5e5e5'
  assign divider_thickness = thickness | default: settings.divider_thickness | default: 1
  assign divider_width = width | default: 'full'
-%}

<div
  class="divider divider--{{ divider_style }} divider--{{ divider_width }}{% if flip %} divider--flip{% endif %}"
  style="--divider-color: {{ divider_color }}; --divider-thickness: {{ divider_thickness }}px;"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  {%- if divider_style == 'wave' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      `preserveAspectRatio="none"` lets the wave stretch to any width without
      the browser letterboxing it, which is what makes one path work from a
      320px phone to a 2560px display.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <svg
      class="divider__wave"
      viewBox="0 0 1200 40"
      preserveAspectRatio="none"
      focusable="false"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      <path
        d="M0,20 C150,0 250,40 400,20 C550,0 650,40 800,20 C950,0 1050,40 1200,20 L1200,40 L0,40 Z"
        fill="var(--divider-color)"
      />
    </svg>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
